<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kim Busik</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1075">1075</a>–1151</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Kim Bu-sik</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kim Bu-sik was a Korean statesman, general and historian of the Goryeo period. In 1135-1136 he suppressed the rebellion of the monk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myocheong">Myocheong</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyongyang">Pyongyang</a>. In retirement he led the compilation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samguk-sagi">Samguk sagi</a>, completed in 1145, the oldest surviving history of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>.</p></div>
